message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "gasm-max-boundary: supplementary code and Lean formalization for the maximum of the lattice for generalized alternating sign matrices"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Kim"
    given-names: "Hwa Kyung"
    email: "indices@smu.ac.kr"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics Education, Sangmyung University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7727-9204"
# After Zenodo issues the DOI, uncomment the two lines below and fill in the number.
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXXX"
# url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXXX"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hwakyungkim/gasm-max-boundary"
abstract: >-
  JavaScript (Node.js) programs that count classes of generalized alternating
  sign matrices directly from the definition and check, on small arrays and
  for the values of Table 1, the main statements of the paper "The maximum of
  the lattice for generalized alternating sign matrices"; and a Lean 4
  (Mathlib) formalization of its main theorem, the folding inequality and the
  folding injection, for all m, n >= 2.
keywords:
  - alternating sign matrix
  - generalized alternating sign matrix
  - six-vertex model
  - height function
  - Lean 4
